        "reason": "Type B cast defect: TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REGEXP_REPLACE(col, offset-strip), \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[.SSSSSS]\") returns NULL on any shape the pinned format misses (date-only values especially), and TRY_ makes it silent -- those NULLs reach the judge as differing_null_only/gap_shaped, i.e. a parse failure disguised as a FHIR coverage gap at the lower bar. Replace every datetime mapping with a bare TRY_CAST(col AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). See pathling-sql SKILL.md and MIMIC_NOTES.md:337.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted attempt 0001's contested unkeyed multiset divergence. The missing FHIR paths are MedicationRequest.dispenseRequest.validityPeriod.start/end: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_request.sql:172-177 omits invalid or incomplete intervals, and authoredOn at :55,124 is pharmacy entertime rather than either source endpoint, so ICU stay_id cannot be reconstructed when starttime is absent. The same ETL at :43-44 irreversibly normalizes DST-gap endpoints through TIMESTAMPTZ (+3600 seconds). Exhaustive EXCEPT ALL pairing accounted for all 43,576 mirrored divergences, with no invented rows; all defensible direct/mix mappings and filters were applied. The judge reported 691,886/735,462 exact tuples (94.075%).",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
